178
00:09:41,666 --> 00:09:46,000
you really don't have much margin for error in this situation

179
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,800
so the suggestion that is given is use two energy hatches

180
00:09:50,266 --> 00:09:53,933
one piece of cable on each of the two energy hatches

181
00:09:54,333 --> 00:09:55,733
do not connect those two

182
00:09:56,333 --> 00:10:03,566
and then you put the turbines in a way that they connect directly to those cables

183
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:08,066
the thing is that each one of those energy hatches can accept two amps

184
00:10:08,966 --> 00:10:12,866
and the machine itself needs four amps at thirty EU per tick

185
00:10:13,066 --> 00:10:14,966
so here you have a loss of one

186
00:10:15,133 --> 00:10:17,500
with one block you already get thirty one

187
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,733
if you lose one more

188
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,566
you have no margin

189
00:10:20,566 --> 00:10:22,366
you are basically net gainer (?)

190
00:10:22,366 --> 00:10:25,266
so if for some reason some packets of power are lost

191
00:10:26,066 --> 00:10:27,733
in the multiblock will fail

192
00:10:28,166 --> 00:10:31,500
you can also add a third energy hatch if you want

193
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:36,500
